{"name":"Shanghai Peach","hex":"#d79a91","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shanghai","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To force or trick someone to go somewhere or do something against their will or interest, particularly:\n\nTo press-gang sailors, especially  for shipping or fishing work.\n\n To trick a suspect into entering a jurisdiction in which they can be lawfully arrested.\n To transfer a serviceman against their will.","To press-gang sailors, especially  for shipping or fishing work."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of chicken with large bodies, long legs, and feathered shanks.","A kind of daub."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shanghai"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shanghai","blocks":[{"text":"Shanghai is a provincial-level direct-administered municipality in China. It has a population of 30,050,000 in the urban area as of 2026, thus making it China's most populous city and more broadly the fifth-largest city in the world by population. The city is located on the southern estuary of the Yangtze River, with the Huangpu River bisecting the city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg/330px-Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_%2832208802494%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg/500px-Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg/1280px-Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg/500px-Shanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShanghai_-_Yu_Garden_-_0035.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg/500px-2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/2024-Apr_Shanghai_East_Nanjing_Road_morning_01.jpg/